-- title:
--   Discriminant is associated to the norm of the Jacobian determinant
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is a Noetherian domain, and let $A$ be a commutative $R$-algebra which is free and finite as an $R$-module. Let $\iota$ be a finite type with decidable equality and $b$ an $R$-basis of $A$ indexed by $\iota$. Let $m$ be a natural number, let $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to R[X_0,\dots,X_{m-1}]$ be an $m$-tuple of polynomials in $m$ variables, and suppose given an isomorphism $e$ of $R$-algebras from $R[X_0,\dots,X_{m-1}]/(f_0,\dots,f_{m-1})$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the range of $f$, onto $A$. The conclusion is that the discriminant $\mathrm{discr}_R(b)$ of the basis $b$, i.e. the determinant of the trace form matrix $(\mathrm{Tr}_{A/R}(b_i b_j))$, and the element $N_{A/R}\bigl(e(\overline{\det(\partial f_i/\partial X_j)})\bigr)$ of $R$ — the norm over $R$ of the image under $e$ of the class modulo $(f_0,\dots,f_{m-1})$ of the determinant of the Jacobian matrix $(\partial f_i/\partial X_j)_{i,j}$ — are associated in $R$, that is, each is the product of the other with a unit of $R$.
--
--   This is the multivariate form of the classical identity expressing the discriminant of a monogenic order as the norm of the derivative of its defining polynomial, valid for a finite free complete intersection presented by $m$ equations in $m$ variables, with the Kähler different represented by the Jacobian determinant. It is used in the computation of the discriminant of rings of integers attached to $p$-divisible groups, via [`PDivisibleGroup.associated_discr_level_of_hasDimension_of_ringOfIntegers`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.associated_discr_level_of_hasDimension_of_ringOfIntegers).
